WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
Already using Codex, Claude, or another coding agent?

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.880
MOMM gives it a review team.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.860
Instead of copying work between separate chats, make one request.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.940
Your selected AI tools challenge the work, and your agent brings the

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:14.960
result back together.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.260
Keep your agent.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.780
Add the review team.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.500
MOMM stands for Mixture of Model Modality.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.364
Think different AI reviewers, working with different kinds of input:

00:00:24.364 --> 00:00:28.614
code, written plans, and, where a reviewer supports it, images or

00:00:28.614 --> 00:00:29.000
documents.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.740
It's not a new model.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.080
It's a way to make your existing tools work together.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.220
The benefit is broader scrutiny.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.494
Ask other tools to challenge an assumption, spot an overlooked risk,

00:00:40.494 --> 00:00:44.380
or suggest a simpler approach before you commit to it.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:48.340
Your current agent remains responsible for investigating and testing

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.220
the advice.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:53.111
You get more challenge, without handing your project to competing

00:00:53.111 --> 00:00:53.500
editors.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.740
If you're manually copying work between chats, you wait for answers,

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.980
compare the replies, then explain the changes back to your agent.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:05.738
MOMM runs selected reviews in parallel and collects them into one

00:01:05.738 --> 00:01:06.080
report.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.580
That's less manual coordination.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:13.163
It can reduce review waiting, although more reviewers still consume

00:01:13.163 --> 00:01:14.080
more quota.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.620
On September fourth, the public development record held three

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:21.947
hundred and two apply decisions, and two hundred and fifty one

00:01:21.947 --> 00:01:22.340
rejections.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.680
Advice was weighed, not just accepted.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:28.740
These are the maintainer's records, not a customer benchmark.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.473
No universal productivity or accuracy percentage has been

00:01:32.473 --> 00:01:32.940
established.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:33.740
Why MOMM?

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:35.680
You choose the provider tools.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.380
Keep the agent you already work in.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:42.480
Inspect the open source protocol and your local decision history.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:46.380
CodeRabbit and Qodo also offer AI review workflows.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.565
MOMM is a fit when you want to coordinate your selected account based

00:01:50.565 --> 00:01:53.140
tools, with one responsible agent and explicit verification.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:54.640
Here's how to start.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.760
You need Git, Node eighteen or newer, and a compatible agent.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.880
Keep the clone in a permanent folder.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.758
Open the MOMM guide, copy the installation and upgrade prompt, and

00:02:04.758 --> 00:02:06.520
paste it into your agent.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.575
It finds the stable release and previews installation for your

00:02:10.575 --> 00:02:10.980
harness.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.140
Approve the plan.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.460
Open the local Setup Center.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:17.940
Choose your current agent, connect a reviewer with its account

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.680
login, and verify the connection.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.208
Start with one; add another when its perspective earns the extra

00:02:24.208 --> 00:02:24.620
quota.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:28.670
The dashboard shows command line versions and guides explicit

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.120
updates.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.220
Provider subscriptions and usage limits still apply.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:34.020
Return to your project.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.120
Choose which providers may receive the work.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.040
Then ask: use MOMM to review my changes.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.862
Investigate findings, verify any fixes, record every decision, and

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.560
show me the ledger.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.240
Your agent handles the review loop.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.060
You don't have to relay each conversation yourself.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:53.300
You're seeing MOMM review this film's own script.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.300
The result isn't just a score.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:58.500
See each reviewer's findings and suggestions together.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.212
Your agent tests material claims, applies changes the evidence

00:03:02.212 --> 00:03:05.100
supports, or rejects advice with a reason.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.320
Unfinished decisions stay visible.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.300
Agreement doesn't replace evidence.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.100
Then open your private ledger.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.780
Who raised the issue?

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.180
What did your agent decide?

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.360
What evidence supports the change?

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:20.780
The report, decisions, and completion record are there to inspect.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:25.380
That makes review easier to revisit, explain, and hand over.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:28.868
Use MOMM for a meaningful change, a difficult decision, or a release

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:29.740
you want challenged.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:34.116
Start small and judge the value on your own work: useful findings,

00:03:34.116 --> 00:03:35.940
review time, and rework avoided.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.100
Open the guide.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.000
Copy the prompt.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.340
Keep your agent.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.151
Add the review team.
